    {
      "id": "ae3342c823ec13cbed3492d1ac779d4cc32ff41e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2665557339,
          "type": null,
          "body": "@JaapKeuter   \nAn empty string (not NULL) help link: ([packet-mac-lte.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-mac-lte.c#L10994), [packet-mac-nr.](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-mac-nr.c#L5541))\n```\n     \"\",  /* TODO: is this ref to help manual? */\n```\n\ndisables the Help button on the the UAT editor:  \n[ui/qt/uat_dialog.cpp](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/ui/qt/uat_dialog.cpp#L134):  \n```\n        if (uat_->help && strlen(uat_->help) > 0) {\n            help_button_->setEnabled(true);\n        }\n```\n\nCan be seen with  \n`mac-lte.drb_table\t\tUnknown\t\tUAT\t\t[Managed in the file \"drb_logchans\"]`  \nand  \n`mac-nr.drb_table\t\tUnknown\t\tUAT\t\t[Managed in the file \"drb_bearerconfig\"]`\n  \nIs this a feature that should be documented?  \nOr not allowed - always have the button go to specific help if written or the generic help otherwise.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
